<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter Claver</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1580–1654</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Pedro Claver</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter Claver was a Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> priest who spent nearly forty years in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cartagena-colombia">Cartagena de Indias</a> ministering to enslaved Africans arriving on slave ships. He met the ships, brought food and medicine, nursed the sick and baptised many thousands. Canonised in 1888, he is the patron saint of slaves and of Colombia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-claver.jpg" alt="Peter Claver" width="202" height="285" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User Andymeyer on en.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:StPeterClaver.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
